Collection in Java
group of similar objects

What is a Framework?
Unified architecture to do something

Collection Framework?
Manipulate and represent java collections  in standard way.
set of classes and interface

Interface :Blueprint of a class

interface Car{
stop();  --> method have no body --> Abstract method
movefwd();
moveBWD();
getKms();
getModel();
}

The class implement method of interface they must have body and implement keyword
all method should be in that class

Implement class c1 {
stop(){}
movefwd(){}
moveBWD(){}
getKms(){}
getModel(){}
}

Collection Framework Hierarchy

Iterable(interface)   ------> Collection<Interface>

have four sub-Interface
List<Interface>     Queue<Interface>   Dequeue<Interface>  Set<Interface>
ArrayList<class>    LinkedList<class>   ArrayDequeue<class> Hashset<class>
linkedList<class>   PriorityQueue<class> LinkedList<class>   LinkedHashSet<class>
Stack<class>                                               SortedSet<Interface>
                                                                  |
                                                             TreeSet<class>

Map<Interface>
HashTable<class>
HashMap<class>
SortedMap<Interface>----> TreeMap<class>


Methods of Collection Interface
add(E e)
clear()
contains(object o)
equals(object o)
remove(object o)
size()

